Create a persistent live card in the calling assistant conversation. Use the same View schema as persona-view and extension UI: sections of components, a required plain-text fallback, and optional named pages. The card stays at its feed position; use view_update to change it. The hub validates the View and returns field-level errors for correction. At most 64 KB per card and 200 cards per conversation. This does not send a push notification. Keep the conclusion in your normal reply too. Returns {id, version}; save the id for updates. Do not collect passwords or secrets in a card.

{"type":"object","required":["view"],"properties":{"view":{"type":"object","description":"A View from schema/extension/view.schema.json with a required plain-text fallback and sections. Only assistant reply/open/push.page/pop actions, not extension ui.action ids."}}}
